  {
    "number": 141,
    "title": "Reconcile desktop-control documentation completion in the guide",
    "body": "Refs #63. Completion follow-up to #140.\n\nPR #140 delivered the desktop-control documentation as `0d1b0930efae23912b942f6e65560763402fe665`. Independent Standards and Specification reviews and all six PR/main jobs passed; issue #63 is closed as completed. Guide issue #35 links the delivered document and marks only that checklist item complete.\n\nRefresh the maintained guide to those verified facts. Retain closed #63 as a reference, remove it from primary open-issue coverage and the remaining-work roadmap, and refresh paginated repository history. The independent qualification path and all downstream preset gates are preserved. No product behavior, OpenSpec capability, architecture viewer or source pin changes.\n\nValidation at head `6bd0e4d3fa25da2e107766292e1a6f878b0ab46d`, base/merge-base `0d1b0930efae23912b942f6e65560763402fe665`:\n\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/build_guide.py` passed: 95 primary open issues, 12 guides, nine unchanged viewers, 52 roadmap nodes and 108 merged PRs.\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/test_maintenance.py` passed all five tests.\n- `node docs/work-guide/work/check_guide.cjs` passed with Node 24.21.0 and installed Playwright/Chromium: six widths, coverage/links, search/navigation, diagram inspection and print expansion/restoration. No page errors or main-page external requests.\n- Rebuilding after commit produced no output drift; `git diff --check` passed. Guide SHA-256 `cec272dbe78cb9ad227f1995a3719249668049869b8d4c19d60fc5386d653ba8`.\n\nAll 12 changed paths are under `docs/work-guide/`. Both unchanged workflows exclude precisely that directory for pull requests and pushes to main. Apply the existing SDLC guide-only CI exception only after current-head run/check readbacks confirm intentional filtering. Independent Standards/Specification reviews and guarded squash remain required. The guide uses the existing UI-approval exemption.\n\nPublic publication remains separate. The public landing page still serves hash `4d8f172a5025252c7b06551dfa862d1abe697fc532a54f75151d231217ed799e`; this PR does not publish it. No installation, hardware/input, application, transport or visible-device acceptance is claimed.\n\nDelivery strategy: coordinator-owned guide edits and two independent reviewers, reusing the Standards and Specification contexts requested at gpt-5.6-terra/high. Three distinct agents used; no implementation workers or advisor consultations. Runtime settings/usage remain unexposed. Source review round 1 passed without corrections; this is guide review round 1.\n",
    "state": "open",
